Task 1: Create a Job Workflow with Dependencies
Subtask 1.1: Prepare Required Job Templates
First, we need to create the individual job templates that will be part of our workflow.

Access the Ansible Automation Platform interface

Open your web browser and navigate to the AWX interface
Log in with the provided credentials
Create the first job template - System Update

Navigate to Templates in the left sidebar
Click Add and select Job Template
Fill in the following details:
Name: System Update Job
Job Type: Run
Inventory: Select your available inventory
Project: Select your project containing playbooks
Playbook: Create or select a system update playbook
Credentials: Select appropriate machine credentials
Create the system update playbook

Create a file named system-update.yml in your project directory:

---
- name: System Update Playbook
  hosts: all
  become: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Update package cache (Ubuntu/Debian)
      apt:
        update_cache: yes
        cache_valid_time: 3600
      when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"
      
    - name: Update package cache (RHEL/CentOS)
      yum:
        update_cache: yes
      when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"
      
    - name: Display system information
      debug:
        msg: "System {{ inventory_hostname }} updated successfully"
        
    - name: Create update completion marker
      file:
        path: /tmp/system_updated
        state: touch
        mode: '0644'
Create the second job template - Application Deployment

Click Add and select Job Template again
Fill in the following details:
Name: Application Deployment Job
Job Type: Run
Inventory: Select the same inventory
Project: Select your project
Playbook: Create or select an application deployment playbook
Create the application deployment playbook

Create a file named app-deployment.yml:

---
- name: Application Deployment Playbook
  hosts: all
  become: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Check if system update completed
      stat:
        path: /tmp/system_updated
      register: update_status
      
    - name: Fail if system not updated
      fail:
        msg: "System update must be completed before application deployment"
      when: not update_status.stat.exists
      
    - name: Install required packages
      package:
        name:
          - nginx
          - git
        state: present
        
    - name: Start and enable nginx
      systemd:
        name: nginx
        state: started
        enabled: yes
        
    - name: Deploy sample application
      copy:
        content: |
          <html>
          <head><title>Workflow Deployment Success</title></head>
          <body>
            <h1>Application Deployed Successfully!</h1>
            <p>Deployed via Ansible Workflow on {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}</p>
          </body>
          </html>
        dest: /var/www/html/index.html
        mode: '0644'
Create the third job template - Health Check

Create another job template named Health Check Job
Use the same inventory and project settings
Create the health check playbook

Create a file named health-check.yml:

---
- name: Health Check Playbook
  hosts: all
  tasks:
    - name: Check nginx service status
      systemd:
        name: nginx
      register: nginx_status
      
    - name: Verify web service response
      uri:
        url: "http://{{ inventory_hostname }}"
        method: GET
        status_code: 200
      register: web_response
      
    - name: Display health check results
      debug:
        msg: |
          Health Check Results:
          - Nginx Status: {{ nginx_status.status.ActiveState }}
          - Web Response: {{ web_response.status }}
          - Health Check: PASSED
          
    - name: Create health check completion marker
      file:
        path: /tmp/health_check_passed
        state: touch
        mode: '0644'
