Task 2: Implement Conditional Logic
Subtask 2.1: Create Conditional Job Templates
Create a rollback job template

Navigate to Templates and create a new job template
Name: Rollback Job
Configure with appropriate settings
Create the rollback playbook

Create a file named rollback.yml:

---
- name: Rollback Playbook
  hosts: all
  become: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Stop nginx service
      systemd:
        name: nginx
        state: stopped
      ignore_errors: yes
      
    - name: Remove application files
      file:
        path: /var/www/html/index.html
        state: absent
        
    - name: Remove update markers
      file:
        path: "{{ item }}"
        state: absent
      loop:
        - /tmp/system_updated
        - /tmp/health_check_passed
        
    - name: Log rollback completion
      debug:
        msg: "Rollback completed successfully on {{ inventory_hostname }}"
Create a notification job template

Create another job template named Notification Job
Create the notification playbook

Create a file named notification.yml:

---
- name: Notification Playbook
  hosts: localhost
  connection: local
  tasks:
    - name: Send success notification
      debug:
        msg: |
          WORKFLOW NOTIFICATION:
          Status: {{ workflow_status | default('SUCCESS') }}
          Timestamp: {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}
          Workflow: Complete Application Deployment
          
    - name: Write notification to file
      copy:
        content: |
          Workflow Execution Report
          ========================
          Status: {{ workflow_status | default('SUCCESS') }}
          Completed: {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}
          Workflow: Complete Application Deployment Workflow
        dest: /tmp/workflow_notification.txt
        mode: '0644'
      delegate_to: localhost
